  "_about": "Who lives in Riverwood, who works or drinks where, and who gets on with whom. Only what vanilla Skyrim shows is here: marriages, family, work, and the courting of Camilla. No friendships or feelings are invented. People are matched by their Skyrim.esm base form ID, so names here are only for reading. A person's gossipiness is not set here: it comes from their Mantella bio, or 0.5 (average) when there is none. A seed entry is written once per person (and once per relationship) and never overwrites anything that already exists in a world. Children (Frodnar, Dorthe) are left out on purpose: Living World never includes child NPCs.",
  "_communities_about": "kind is one of settlement, household, faction, guild. Gossip treats every 'household' as a group whose members see each other daily (high contact), so the inn and the mill use that kind for the people who work or spend their days there, not because they are families. role is a plain description. influence is how much others weigh this person's views when the town-wide summary is averaged; every member starts at 0.5 (average) because the game does not say otherwise. It never sets anyone's own opinion. Nobody's opinion is set by a community: each person forms their own from what they see and hear.",
