  "_relationships_about": "Starting numbers follow one rule per kind of tie (spouse 0.8/0.8/0.6, sibling or parent 0.7/0.7/0.4, uncle or aunt 0.5/0.6/0.4, rival -0.4/-0.5/-0.3, courting 0.4/0.7/0.3 with attraction 0.7, undecided side 0.3/0.3/0.2; familiarity 1.0 for people in one home, else 0.7), because the game shows the tie but not its strength. Numbers are the starting point (-1..1 for trust, affinity, respect; 0..1 for familiarity); everything that happens in play is added on top. An entry without \"one_way\" gives both people the same numbers. Where two people feel differently about each other, there are two \"one_way\" entries, one per direction. kinship and status are what b is to a (\"a\": \"sven\", \"b\": \"hilde\", \"kinship\": \"parent\" means Hilde is Sven's parent); \"back\" gives what a is to b when that differs. Courting is only ever one person's side: it says nothing about whether the other returns the interest.",
